**Key findings summary**:

- **1 high**: `SocGate` has no hysteresis (single threshold), risking rapid on/off cycling at the threshold boundary
- **2 medium**: Solar tracking doesn't distinguish forecast vs. actual PV; temperature-dependent efficiency is not applied to charge-time estimates (only to driving consumption)
- **6 low**: Time window implicit ≤24h span constraint, log-normal used at actor layer not preference layer, `SocTarget` naming vs. actual ready-by responsibility, percentile rounding granularity, composer target_soc provenance decoupling, and an OCHRE comparison note
